# The published ruleset is hashed byte-for-byte: docs/BASELINE.md carries a SHA-256 over the exact
# bytes of the file, and `pnpm check:baseline` recomputes it from the working tree. Without this,
# a checkout with core.autocrlf=true would convert LF to CRLF, hash different bytes, and fail the
# integrity check on a clean tree — the guard reporting a corrupted artifact when nothing was
# touched. Pinning EOLs keeps the published definition ("SHA-256 over the file bytes") true on
# every platform rather than trading it for a checkout-dependent one.
#
# Anything else that gains a checksum row in the manifest needs pinning here too.
rules/*.json text eol=lf
